# Behavioral suite manifest — one line per suite:   tier|type|file|label
#
# tier — how central the suite is; it decides when the suite runs:
#   essential       fastest proof the system is alive and the core path works
#   core            the everyday regression set
#   extended        slower or less central functional suites
#   security        authorization, input validation, abuse and hardening checks
#   integration     suites that cross a boundary (third-party, queue, webhook)
#   performance     latency and throughput assertions (not the k6 load harness)
#   infrastructure  migrations, configuration, deployment shape
#   recent          suites for work still settling; promoted to another tier later
#
# type — what kind of test it is, which is a different question from how
# central it is. Free-form, so a project can name its own; the conventional
# values are:
#   unit, e2e, static, backend, ui, browser, api
#
# Modes (tier selection):
#   --quick     essential
#   --standard  essential + core + extended
#   --full      every tier
#
# --tier <name> runs one tier; --type <name> narrows to one type, and the two
# compose:  --tier essential --type unit
#
# Files are relative to the project's suites directory. A listed file that does
# not exist is reported as SKIP, never as a pass.
#
# The older three-field form `tier|file|label` still reads — such a line simply
# has no type, and --type never selects it.
#
# Example rows — replace with your own:
#
# essential|api|health-and-readiness.sh|Health & Readiness
# essential|e2e|core-write-path.sh|Create, read back, verify persisted
# core|api|users-crud.sh|Users CRUD
# core|api|search-filters.sh|Search & Filtering
# core|ui|signup-form.sh|Signup form renders and submits
# extended|backend|reporting-exports.sh|Reporting Exports
# security|api|input-validation.sh|Input Validation
# security|api|authorization-matrix.sh|Authorization Matrix
# integration|e2e|outbound-webhooks.sh|Outbound Webhooks
# performance|api|list-endpoint-latency.sh|List Endpoint Latency
# infrastructure|static|migrations-applied.sh|Migrations Applied
# recent|browser|wip-feature-flags.sh|Feature Flags (new)
